            <p>A Costa Rica cruise allows visitors to explore one of the world's most bio diverse nations in the comfort of a modern vessel. Costa Rica is famous for its rainforests, intriguing volcanoes, exotic wildlife and stunning beaches. Approaching from the sea also has the added bonus of being beautiful; verdant green scenes have sprung up on the horizon well before you make landfall. </p>

            <p>Costa Rica is not a typical lazy beach vacation spot. You can get up early in the morning to spot exotic birds and wildlife in a rainforest, and then spend the afternoon on an empty beach. A Costa Rica cruise will take you to this natural wonderland without needing to think about how you'll get from one area to another. </p>

            <h2>Cruises That Go to Costa Rica</h2>

            <p>You will find that many of the more established cruise lines offer cruises to Costa Rica as part of their Central America or Panama Canal routes. <a href="https://www.fareschoices.com/royal-caribbean-cruises.aspx">Royal Caribbean</a>, <a href="https://www.fareschoices.com/norwegian-cruise-line.aspx"> Norwegian Cruise Line </a>, <a href="https://www.fareschoices.com/princess-cruises.aspx"> Princess Cruises </a>, <a href="https://www.fareschoices.com/holland-america-cruises.aspx"> Holland America Line </a>, <a href="https://www.fareschoices.com/celebrity-cruise-line.aspx"> Celebrity Cruises </a>, <a href="https://www.fareschoices.com/msc-cruise-line.aspx"> MSC Cruises </a>, <a href="https://www.fareschoices.com/regent-seven-seas-cruise-line.aspx"> Regent Seven Seas </a>, <a href="https://www.fareschoices.com/seabourn-cruise-line.aspx"> Seabourn Cruise Line </a>, and <a href="https://www.fareschoices.com/silversea-cruises.aspx"> Silversea Cruises </a> are common cruise lines with Costa Rican destinations in Puntarenas or Puerto Limon. </p>

            <p>Cruises that visit Costa Rica tend to emphasize active experiences over crowds or city stops. Wildlife, scenery, and cultural visits are a priority. It's something that has made Costa Rica an interesting destination for the nature reservationist-minded traveler. </p>

            <h2>7 Day Cruises to Costa Rica</h2>

            <p>For those who want a mix, 7 day cruises to Costa Rica is the perfect length of time. They usually are a mix of lazy days at sea and a couple of port calls in Central America. Guests are welcome to do some and see more of Costa Rica while also visiting neighbors such as Panama or Nicaragua. </p>

            <p>The best thing about our 7-day cruises is the flexibility. They also provide sufficient time to go on rainforest, coffee, and beach excursions without having to rush. Yet, at the same time, it's long enough to accommodate most holiday plans. </p>

            <h2> About Costa Rica and Panama Canal Cruises</h2>

            <p> Travelers can experience the engineering feat that is the Panama Canal, while also soaking in Costa Rica's natural beauty. This means a journey that combines history and natural beauty. Cruising a Costa Rica & Panama Canal itinerary, cruisers may traverse rich tropical terrain past tranquil shoreline waters. Passing through from the Pacific to the Caribbean side of the canal is what makes it on the “To Do” list. This itinerary is highly favored by passengers who appreciate both scenic cruising and enrichment. </p>

            <h2>Costa Rica Cruises Depart from Regional ports</h2>

            <p>Aside from ships that sail to the country, there are also cruises aboard Costa Rica's waters departing from their port. These cruises usually stick to nearby Central American coasts or skirt the Panama Canal and Caribbean islands. Leaving from Costa Rica puts its travelers in the natural beauty. </p>

            <p>Cruises from Costa Rica. International cruisers and local travelers can take advantage of cruises from Costa Rica. If you begin your journey in Costa Rica, you can also add extra time before or after the cruise to explore inland rainforests, volcanoes, and national parks. </p>

            <h2>Life Onboard And  Preparation For Visiting Costa Rica</h2>

            <p>Life on your cruise ship dictates the tone of the journey before you even set foot in Costa Rica. From onboard ship classes and gifts to gourmet dining, entertainment, and relaxation, there are options sure to please everyone aboard the ships of Royal Caribbean International, Norwegian Cruise Lines, Princess Cruises, Holland America Line®, and MSC Cruises. Guests can sit in on cultural lectures about Central America or just relax by the pool. </p>

            <p>Upscale cruise line operators such as Regent Seven Seas, Seabourn Cruise Line, and Silversea Cruises offer a more personal experience with varying levels of service. Regardless of which cruise line you select, the ship is a welcome reprieve following each day of exploration in Costa Rica. </p>

            <h2>Shore Excursions and Wildlife Adventures</h2>

            <p>Afterward, excursions focus on the country's diverse wildlife at the port in Costa Rica. Travelers can visit rainforests teeming with monkeys and sloths, explore volcanic terrain, or relax on beaches shaded by palm trees. Many guided tours have knowledgeable naturalists who describe the ecosystem to you. </p>

            <p>Those into more adventurous pursuits can opt for zip lining, river rafting, or trekking in national parks. Some may opt for a tranquil boat ride through mangroves along the coast. Read more, the possible experiences are as diverse as life itself, so no matter your interests, every traveller is sure to create at least one unforgettable memory while on a cruise to Costa Rica. </p>

